# Local CV Builder — Architecture Rules

## Stack
- Frontend: React + TypeScript + Tailwind + Zustand
- Backend: Tauri 2 + Rust
- Database: SQLite via rusqlite (local app data dir)
- AI: Ollama (localhost only) with rule-based fallback

## Folder Conventions

| Layer | Path | Naming |
|-------|------|--------|
| React components | `src/components/` | PascalCase |
| React pages | `src/pages/` | PascalCase |
| State stores | `src/state/` | camelCase files (`useCvStore.ts`) |
| CV templates | `src/templates/cv/` | kebab-case |
| Rust commands | `src-tauri/src/commands.rs` | snake_case functions |
| Database | `src-tauri/src/db/` | schema.rs, models.rs, queries.rs |
| Export | `src-tauri/src/export/` | PDF pipeline |
| NLP | `src-tauri/src/nlp/` | Ollama + fallback |
| Scrapers | `src-tauri/src/scrapers/` | snake_case modules |

## Constraints

- **Local-first**: No cloud AI APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.)
- **Privacy**: No telemetry, no remote logging
- **Modularity**: One concern per module; vertical slices over horizontal layers
- **Network**: HTTP only for user-initiated scraping (job boards) and localhost Ollama

## Adding New Features

Use the `module-generator` skill in `.cursor/skills/module-generator/SKILL.md`.

## Error Handling

- Rust: `AppResult<T>` with `AppError` enum
- Frontend: try/catch on `invoke()` with user-visible messages
